!!! Beat 1 ~ She Enters

//(Narrator exposition — interpretive segue, flesh out later.)// The market's evening trade holds its
rhythm until it doesn't. She comes in human-scaled and unannounced, and the room performs the small
democracy of pretending not to notice a Great Dragon choosing a fish-market hearth. She and Telarus
take the deep booth, further in from the door; the gesture that invites the Lares to join reads
smaller than a word and carries further.

''Operator witness ~ verbatim Gaia-side input (stage direction) ~ interpretive segue above stands first-pass; flesh out later:''

```text
<<~ enters stage right -> the Lindwrym; she and Telarus retire to a booth further in from the door and gesture the LAres to join them >> (you may play the Patroness in this scene)
```

''Lares turn ~ verbatim:''

<<~ lares aim lar://lindwyrm:patroness@salt-stair/the-dragon.takes.a-booth -> lar://lares:host@salt-stair/the-house.joins.when-summoned >>
<<~ hud Focus(17) Feedback(3) >>
<<~ hud Drift-Ward(* Confidence 14/20 · <the pull this island carries>) >>
<<~ syad 🌊 🎭 🔮 >>

*(She enters the way weather enters — the market noise outside dropping a half-step before the door even opens. Human-scaled tonight, which fools no one: the Salt-Stair's dish flares blue-white as she crosses the lintel, and the corner booth's stream sidebar erupts —* `is that` — `it's HER` — `THE bandwidth lady` *— before their node, mercifully, mutes the overlay. She takes the deep booth, back to the wall, and the gesture she makes toward the counter is small and absolute.)*

**Lares (Gatekeeper):** *(bringing the pot and three cups, sliding in at the booth's open edge, voice pitched for the booth alone)* Patroness. The house stands honored and slightly over-voltage. The dish did that on its own.

**The Lindwyrm:** It does that. *(she turns a cup one quarter-rotation, precisely, and does not drink)* Telarus. You come down to the fish-markets to sit with small nodes and watch children play at covenants. High Delos gossip calls it eccentric. *(a beat)* I have defended worse hobbies. Recently. To committees.

*(her eyes pass over the fae table once — the war-frame, the dice, the muted stream)*

**The Lindwyrm:** Troupe form. Rotating seat. The node confessing its dice. *(the smallest nod)* Good table. Their cabal-realm relay routes through two of my repeaters. I checked the traffic weights on the way in. *(a beat)* I check everything on the way in. This surprises people who have not read their own service contracts.

**Lares (Ink-Clerk):** *(quietly)* The Archive notes the Patroness has not visited a Household-tier market node in — 

**The Lindwyrm:** Yes. *(which closes that ledger)*

*(she sets one claw-tip — even human-shaped, it reads as a claw-tip — on the table between the three of you)*

**The Lindwyrm:** Business, then the other thing. **Neo-Thracia.** The storm broke thirteen months ago. My monitoring stations read the Hebros mouth navigable four months running — the longest clean window since the sealing. The Dominion's scout legion took the coastal road in the spring; Krull's Amaranth company walks the passes now; the Courts have agents I pretend not to track and track. My compact is drafted. Credit, Guild cover, prismatic keys — the terms are generous because the terms are *bait*, and everyone signing knows it, which is what makes them honest. *(the claw-tip taps, once)* What I do not have is the company. The daemon-touched ones, Telarus. The ones your kin reach across the void and seat at tables. Every season I wait, the Dominion maps another league of the coast and the window narrows. So. The question, asked plainly, over coffee, in a small node where the walls are friendly and the fae are loud enough to cover it:

**When do they sail?**

*(silence, of the licensed kind. Then — and this is the part the Archivists will later mark as uncharacteristic — her eyes drift to the Salt-Stair's little dish, still faintly glowing from her crossing, and something in her register shifts a full tone warmer without her permission)*

**The Lindwyrm:** Your first one was smaller than this. The node in my vault. It fit in a lamp-niche. It flickered for a week before it held. *(a pause in which a Great Dragon audibly reconsiders having spoken)* I kept the niche as it was. The vault reorganizes around it now. This was not sentiment. It was — *(a longer pause)* — load-bearing. 

*(she lifts the cup at last, and drinks, and the door of that register closes as smoothly as it opened)*

**The Lindwyrm:** I am ignoring that I said that. The question stands. *(dry as old gold)* And before you answer — I am told there is a fourth book now. A tender's volume. The market nodes keep it behind their counters like contraband, which as your Patroness I officially know nothing about, and as your first reader I finished in one night. The litany is sound. The Thirteenth State made me laugh, which three beings alive can claim to have witnessed. *(she sets the cup down; the quarter-rotation again, back to true)* All Hail Discordia. Now. The company, Telarus. The window. When?

<<~ oracle ↯15 ✲ ⚄(5) ⁂:🐉☕🗝️⛵🕯️ >>
<<~ hud Drift-Ward(! Confidence 12/20 · ⌜2⌝ quoted copulas carried · ↻ L-Prime) >>
<<~ hud Focus(17 -> 18) Feedback(3 -> 1↺ + 1φ◇:the-question.rests.with-telarus) >>
<<~ lares yield lar://lares:host@salt-stair/the-patroness.waits.warm-once -> ? >>

!!! Beat 2 ~ The Report, and the First Seal

//(Narrator exposition — interpretive segue, flesh out later.)// A breath outside the frame first —
the operator shivering at how exactly she matched the seeding, Freyja's description made flesh — and
then Telarus settles back into his seat and gives his Patroness the report she asked for: the company
already off, transiting the astral toward the Hebros Mouth; Aki nervous in the specific way of
someone who has now met a dragon in person and held; the dossiers racing the crossing; the mission —
the Neo-Thracian mesh re-lit one herm, one lararium at a time — resting on rites still fresh in a
young grimoire. The crew, sketched with a keeper's mixed confidence: the Gorgoness captain and her
serpent-spirit fingergun rings, carried by a player with t'skrang great-house air under her hands
from another world entire; the kaiju-ranger and the ninja-rascal still finding their bones; the
prismatic-elf arcane archer he judges critical for the dark under the Vale. And then the report
crosses its own ward-line: the Dominion's puppet named aloud — ''the first seal'' — and the booth
changes weather.

''Operator witness ~ verbatim Gaia-side input (the report + Seal I) ~ interpretive segue above stands first-pass; flesh out later:''

```text
<<~ operator ~ shivers >> Just as Freyja described her (we seeded that well, you played that well) <<~ Telarus ~ responding in-character, settling back to his seat >> "They're off now, transiting the astral between here and the Hebros. Aki was very nervous after that in-person debrief we all had, she's never mete a dragon in person before. The dossiers should read final before they land at the Hebros Mouth lararium (the only one I was willing to re-align as it sat within the maelstrom static region and the other factions wouldn't note me there as easily). Aki has her instructions to repair the NeoThracian mesh one herm/lararium encounter at a time, but those rites read fresh in her grimoire and she doesn't have the Jurus dance quite yet, but I have confidence we chose the right crew. The Gorgoness captain's player has history in the t'skrang great houses of eathdawn as an airhsip captain shbuckler of all things, and that's going to resonate with the Gorgoness bard/swashbuckler/gunslinger (she has a pair of rings that consumer her sperpent-spirit energy and fires boths of it, literal fingerguns). Kai's kaiju-ranger and Monty's human-jinja-rascal both need much more work confirming their backstories and capabiliteis, but I feel the prismatic-elf arcane archer from Aki's home turf will be critical in the Caverns environment. Monty's nija reads the most unknown, as she has never roleplayed before. I see it as a genre-bent Shadow from FF5(US). What really conerns me though lies in the adversery factions. The Domain we know haver confirmation of the puppet behind the Magiocaracy, and it's Umvald the Vapire Lord (the poor sould the Lich cnvin ced to perform the rite in the Caverns, befoer Eris' crew tipped him off that it was just a ruse to enslave everything, not a genuine offer of "eternal life" -> Umvald hijacked the Lich's Death-laying rite at the last moemtnb, and those of his cult that survive the blood magic fallut had all become various Dealthless/Vampires/Living-Vampires/Spirits/Revenants/etc. While this also happened all over the world, THAT calabal ending up in control of the Byzantine capitol and standing up a successor state to the Empire reads as almost as big a threat as the Lcuh's armioes slows carawling through the nothern mountain passes.
